      "kind": "section",
      "label": "The site and its sitemap",
      "excerpt": "The site and its sitemap",
      "text": "actually, I think the site references the pages, so e.g. the page names can be translated or moved",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T17:42:56.683Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:23.305Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  the site file now holds each page's address, name and parameters, and a page file holds only what it shows and does.  So a page moves or gets a translated name without changing the page;  links name the page and the site makes the address (Overview 1.3, marked).</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:09.577Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "o5",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "A page: its jobs, then its mockup",
      "excerpt": "A page: its jobs, then its mockup",
      "text": "the jobs bit should persist.  Should optionall express of the \"jobs\" as Agile Stories",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-07T17:44:03.680Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:24.211Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  a page's jobs are saved with it for good, into the real site, and each may be written as an Agile story (\"As a ..., I want ..., so that ...\"), with its \"done when\" checks under it (Overview 1.5, marked).  It becomes its own phase, Page Jobs.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-07T17:45:10.312Z"
      }
    }
  },
